WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.403 --> 00:00:04.478
Unit twenty-four. Contributing to Open Source!

2
00:00:05.417 --> 00:00:09.770
Hello, everyone! I'm Mr. Daniel, your technology teacher.

3
00:00:09.820 --> 00:00:13.729
Hi, Mr. Daniel! What do we learn today?

4
00:00:13.779 --> 00:00:18.106
Today we learn about Contributing to Open Source. Let's go!

5
00:00:19.017 --> 00:00:23.509
Open source. Say it with me. Open source!

6
00:00:27.017 --> 00:00:31.217
Repository. Say it with me. Repository!

7
00:00:34.698 --> 00:00:38.250
Issue. Say it with me. Issue!

8
00:00:41.701 --> 00:00:45.101
Fork. Say it with me. Fork!

9
00:00:48.623 --> 00:00:52.547
Pull request. Say it with me. Pull request!

10
00:00:56.131 --> 00:00:59.857
Review. Say it with me. Review!

11
00:01:03.306 --> 00:01:07.539
Documentation. Say it with me. Documentation!

12
00:01:11.013 --> 00:01:14.629
Community. Say it with me. Community!

13
00:01:18.168 --> 00:01:31.275
To contribute to open source, find an issue in a repository, fork it, make changes, and open a pull request. Maintainers review it. Improving documentation is a great first contribution to the community.

14
00:01:31.325 --> 00:01:34.822
Now I understand. Thank you, Mr. Daniel!

15
00:01:35.872 --> 00:01:41.307
Look! What's the word?

16
00:01:41.357 --> 00:01:42.507
Issue!

17
00:01:43.460 --> 00:01:48.770
Look! What's the word?

18
00:01:48.820 --> 00:01:50.148
Documentation!

19
00:01:51.138 --> 00:01:57.867
Did you know? Fixing spelling mistakes in documentation is a real and welcome open source contribution!

20
00:01:57.917 --> 00:02:00.157
Wow! I did not know that!

21
00:02:01.300 --> 00:02:10.009
Think and answer. What could be your first open source contribution?

22
00:02:10.059 --> 00:02:11.209
Great answer!

23
00:02:12.292 --> 00:02:17.817
Great job today! Keep learning, and see you next time. Goodbye!

24
00:02:17.867 --> 00:02:21.029
Goodbye, everyone! See you next time!

